DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _P_s_r_e_s_i_z_e rescales and centres a document on a different size of  paper.
       The  input PostScript file should follow the Adobe Document Structuring
       Conventions.

       The _-_w option gives the output paper width, and the _-_h option gives the
       output  paper  height,  normally specified in ccmm or iinn to convert Post‐
       Script's points (1/72 of an inch) to centimeters or inches.  The _-_p op‐
       tion can be used as an alternative, to set the output paper size to aa00,,
       aa11,, aa22,, aa33,, aa44,, aa55,, bb55,, lleetttteerr,, lleeggaall,, ttaabbllooiidd,,  ssttaatteemmeenntt,,  executive,
       folio, quarto or 1100xx1144..  The default output paper size is aa44..

       The  _-_W option gives the input paper width, and the _-_H option gives the
       input paper height.  The _-_P option can be used as  an  alternative,  to
       set the input paper size.  The default input paper size is aa44..

       _P_s_r_e_s_i_z_e  normally  prints the page numbers of the pages output; the _-_q
       option suppresses this.

